<http://data.silknow.org/object/59706b8c-4d1a-3113-8d40-4eaff38143e1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A forehead cloth of linen, embroidered with silk thread in shades of blue, red, green, yellow, pink, black and white in detached buttonhole stitch and couching, and silver and silver-gilt thread in plaited braid stitch, chain stitch and couching, with silver spangles.  The pattern consists of scrolling stems bearing carnations, honeysuckle, pansy, roses, cornflower, strawberries, pear, and grapes, with caterpillars and a moth and wasp.  The triangular shape of the forehead cloth is outlined with red silk in stem stitch.  The forehead cloth is unlined. It is unfinished, the edges raw and unturned, and damaged, with one corner torn off."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/59706b8c-4d1a-3113-8d40-4eaff38143e1> .

